From 747c06c3d1e121d53f2aea6fd2b27f974e6c6cf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:16:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: clear a sync MAC's static flag when its L2VNI is
 removed

When zebra deletes the MACs of an L2VNI, it first writes each static
local MAC as a normal entry (force_clear_static), so that the kernel
entry stops being static. zebra_evpn_sync_mac_dp_install() defers any
write for a MAC on an Ethernet Segment until the ES-EVI exists, and an
L2VNI that goes down or is deleted drops its ES-EVIs
(zebra_evpn_vl_vxl_deref()) before it deletes its MACs. So the write is
skipped, the MAC is freed, and the kernel entry stays static: it does
not age, and keeps sending the host's traffic to that port. In SONiC's
FPM MAC sync mode, dplane_fpm_sonic also keeps the MAC's static entry
in the ASIC, which it ends on this write.

The deferral, from commit 09de6e4550, is for sync MACs that bgpd sends
while an ES is being re-added: zebra_evpn_es_evi_mac_install() installs
them once the ES-EVI is created. A MAC being deleted gets no such
second attempt, so do not defer the write that clears its static flag.

Signed-off-by: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
---
 zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
index 0d88150f17..7a50e8cab2 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.c
@@ -1398,9 +1398,11 @@ int zebra_evpn_sync_mac_dp_install(struct zebra_mac *mac, bool set_inactive,
 	struct interface *br_ifp;
 
 	/* If the ES-EVI doesn't exist defer install. When the ES-EVI is
-	 * created we will attempt to install the mac entry again
+	 * created we will attempt to install the mac entry again. A MAC
+	 * being deleted gets no such attempt, so clearing its static flag
+	 * is not deferred: the entry would stay static.
 	 */
-	if (mac->es) {
+	if (mac->es && !force_clear_static) {
 		struct zebra_evpn_es_evi *es_evi;
 
 		es_evi = zebra_evpn_es_evi_find(mac->es, mac->zevpn);
